[{"id":"smq-year2-2.09-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>For each of the following, expand up to and including the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> term, stating in each case the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for which the expansions are valid:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1+x)^{\\frac14}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1+2x)^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{1-3x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2+x)^{-3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(9+3x)^{\\frac12}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{16-36x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt[3]{8-2x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{\\sqrt{3+2x}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1+x)^{\\frac14} \\approx1+\\tfrac14x+\\tfrac12(\\tfrac14)(-\\tfrac34)x^2+\\tfrac16(\\tfrac14)(-\\tfrac34)(-\\tfrac74)x^3+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx1+\\tfrac14x-\\tfrac3{32}x^2+\\tfrac7{128}x^3+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|x|&lt;1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1+2x)^{-1} \\approx1-2x+\\tfrac12(-1)(-2)(2x)^2+\\tfrac16(-1)(-2)(-3)(2x)^3+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx1-2x+4x^2-8x^3+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|2x|&lt;1\\Rightarrow|x|&lt;\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1-3x)^{\\frac12} \\approx1+\\tfrac12(-3x)+\\tfrac12(\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac12)(-3x)^2+\\tfrac16(\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac32)(-3x)^3+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx1-\\tfrac32x-\\tfrac98x^2-\\tfrac{27}{16}x^3+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|3x|&lt;1\\Rightarrow|x|&lt;\\frac13\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2+x)^{-3}=2^{-3}(1+\\frac12x)^{-3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\tfrac18[1-3(\\tfrac12x)+\\tfrac12(-3)(-4)(\\tfrac12x)^2+\\tfrac16(-3)(-4)(-5)(\\tfrac12x)^3+\\ldots]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\tfrac18-\\tfrac3{16}x+\\tfrac3{16}x^2-\\tfrac5{32}x^3+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|\\frac12x|&lt;1\\Rightarrow|x|&lt;2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(9+3x)^{\\frac12}=9^{\\frac12}(1+\\frac13x)^{\\frac12}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx3[1+\\tfrac12(\\tfrac13x)+\\tfrac12(\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac12)(\\tfrac13x)^2+\\tfrac16(\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac32)(\\tfrac13x)^3+\\ldots]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx3+\\tfrac12x-\\tfrac1{24}x^2+\\tfrac1{144}x^3+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|\\frac13x|&lt;1\\Rightarrow|x|&lt;3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(16-36x)^{\\frac12}=16^{\\frac12}(1-\\frac94x)^{\\frac12}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx4[1+\\tfrac12(-\\tfrac94x)+\\tfrac12(\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac94x)^2+\\tfrac16(\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac32)(-\\tfrac94x)^3+\\ldots]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx4-\\tfrac92x-\\tfrac{81}{32}x^2-\\tfrac{729}{256}x^3+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|\\frac94x|&lt;1\\Rightarrow|x|&lt;\\frac49\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">g)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(8-2x)^{\\frac13}=8^{\\frac13}(1-\\frac14x)^{\\frac13}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx2[1+\\tfrac13(-\\tfrac14x)+\\tfrac12(\\tfrac13)(-\\tfrac23)(-\\tfrac14x)^2+\\tfrac16(\\tfrac13)(-\\tfrac23)(-\\tfrac53)(-\\tfrac14x)^3+\\ldots]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx2-\\tfrac16x-\\tfrac1{72}x^2-\\tfrac5{2592}x^3+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|\\frac14x|&lt;1\\Rightarrow|x|&lt;4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">h)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3+2x)^{-\\frac12}=3^{-\\frac12}(1+\\frac23x)^{-\\frac12}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\tfrac1{\\sqrt3}[1-\\tfrac12(\\tfrac23x)+\\tfrac12(-\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac32)(\\tfrac23x)^2+\\tfrac16(-\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac32)(-\\tfrac52)(\\tfrac23x)^3+\\ldots]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\tfrac1{\\sqrt3}-\\tfrac1{3\\sqrt3}x+\\tfrac1{6\\sqrt3}x^2-\\tfrac5{54\\sqrt3}x^3+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =\\tfrac{\\sqrt3}3-\\tfrac{\\sqrt3}9x+\\tfrac{\\sqrt3}{18}x^2-\\tfrac{5\\sqrt3}{162}x^3+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|\\frac23x|&lt;1\\Rightarrow|x|&lt;\\frac32\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.09-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>Write down the coefficient of the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> term in each of the following expansions:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1+3x)^{\\frac14}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1-2x)^{\\frac23}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1+\\frac x2)^{-\\frac34}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{4!}\\times\\frac14(-\\frac34)(-\\frac74)(-\\frac{11}4)(3x)^4=-\\frac{6237}{2048}x^4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. So the coefficient is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\frac{6237}{2048}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{4!}\\times\\frac23(-\\frac13)(-\\frac43)(-\\frac73)(-2x)^4=-\\frac{112}{243}x^4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. So the coefficient is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\frac{112}{243}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{4!}\\times-\\frac34(-\\frac74)(-\\frac{11}4)(-\\frac{15}4)(\\frac12x)^4=\\frac{1155}{32768}x^4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. So the coefficient is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{1155}{32768}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.09-q3","number":3,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the first 3 terms in the expansion of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{\\sqrt{9+x}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence find the first 3 terms in the expansion of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{\\sqrt{9-x^2}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(9+x)^{-\\frac12}=9^{-\\frac12}(1+\\frac19x)^{-\\frac12}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\tfrac13[1-\\tfrac12(\\tfrac19x)+\\tfrac12(-\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac32)(\\tfrac19x)^2+\\ldots]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\tfrac13-\\tfrac1{54}x+\\tfrac1{648}x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(9-x^2)^{-\\frac12} \\approx\\tfrac13-\\tfrac1{54}(-x^2)+\\tfrac1{648}(-x^2)^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\tfrac13+\\tfrac1{54}x^2+\\tfrac1{648}x^4+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.09-q4","number":4,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the expansion of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1+x)^{-\\frac12}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> up to and including the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> term.</p></li><li><p>Hence find the first 3 terms in the expansion of</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1+\\tfrac25x)^{-\\frac12}\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\\sqrt{\\frac{10}{5+2x}}\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1+x)^{-\\frac12} \\approx1-\\tfrac12x+\\tfrac12(-\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac32)x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx1-\\tfrac12x+\\tfrac38x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1+\\tfrac25x)^{-\\frac12} \\approx1-\\tfrac12(\\tfrac25x)+\\tfrac38(\\tfrac25x)^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx1-\\tfrac15x+\\tfrac3{50}x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{10}(5+2x)^{-\\frac12} =\\sqrt{10}\\times\\tfrac1{\\sqrt5}(1+\\tfrac25x)^{-\\frac12}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\sqrt2[1-\\tfrac15x+\\tfrac3{50}x^2+\\ldots]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\sqrt2-\\tfrac{\\sqrt2}5x+\\tfrac{3\\sqrt2}{50}x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.09-q5","number":5,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the first 3 terms in the expansion of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{9-x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence find an approximation to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt8\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(9-x)^{\\frac12}=9^{\\frac12}(1-\\frac19x)^{\\frac12}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx3[1+\\tfrac12(-\\tfrac19x)+\\tfrac{\\frac12(-\\frac12)}2(-\\tfrac19x)^2+\\ldots]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx3-\\tfrac16x-\\tfrac1{216}x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|\\frac19x|&lt;1\\Rightarrow|x|&lt;9\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so can use <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sqrt8=\\sqrt{9-1}\\approx3-\\tfrac16-\\tfrac1{216}+\\ldots\\approx\\tfrac{611}{216}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.09-q6","number":6,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Expand <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1+5x)^{\\frac13}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> up to and including the term in <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Hence find an approximation to the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt[3]{1.1125}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to 4 decimal places.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1+5x)^{\\frac13} \\approx1+\\tfrac13(5x)+\\tfrac12(\\tfrac13)(-\\tfrac23)(5x)^2+\\tfrac16(\\tfrac13)(-\\tfrac23)(-\\tfrac53)(5x)^3+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx1+\\tfrac53x-\\tfrac{25}9x^2+\\tfrac{625}{81}x^3+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1+5x=1.1125\\Rightarrow x=\\frac9{400}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|\\frac15x|&lt;1\\Rightarrow|x|&lt;5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so can use <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac9{400}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sqrt[3]{1.1125} \\approx1+\\tfrac53(\\tfrac9{400})-\\tfrac{25}9(\\tfrac9{400})^2+\\tfrac{625}{81}(\\tfrac9{400})^3+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\tfrac{21221}{20480}\\approx1.0362\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.09-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>By finding the first 3 terms in the expansion of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2-3x)^{\\frac12}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> use <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac1{10}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to find an approximation for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{170}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a value to be found.</p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2-3x)^{\\frac12}=2^{\\frac12}(1-\\frac32x)^{\\frac12}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\sqrt2[1+\\tfrac12(-\\tfrac32x)+\\tfrac12(\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac32x)^2+\\ldots]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\sqrt2-\\tfrac{3\\sqrt2}4x-\\tfrac{9\\sqrt2}{32}x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|\\frac32x|&lt;1\\Rightarrow|x|&lt;\\frac23\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac1{10}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is valid.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{\\tfrac{17}{10}} \\approx\\sqrt2-\\tfrac{3\\sqrt2}4\\times\\tfrac1{10}-\\tfrac{9\\sqrt2}{32}\\times\\tfrac1{100}+\\ldots=\\tfrac{2951}{3200}\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{170} =10\\times\\sqrt{\\tfrac{17}{10}}\\approx10\\times\\tfrac{2951}{3200}\\sqrt2=\\tfrac{2951}{320}\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.09-q8","number":8,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the first 3 terms in the expansions of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1+3x)^{\\frac12}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1+x)^{-\\frac12}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence, show that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{\\frac{1+3x}{1+x}}\\approx1+x-\\frac32x^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li><li><p>State the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for which the expansion is valid.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1+3x)^{\\frac12} \\approx1+\\tfrac12(3x)+\\tfrac12(\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac12)(3x)^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx1+\\tfrac32x-\\tfrac98x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|3x|&lt;1\\Rightarrow|x|&lt;\\frac13\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1+x)^{-\\frac12} \\approx1-\\tfrac12x+\\tfrac12(-\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac32)x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx1-\\tfrac12x+\\tfrac38x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|x|&lt;1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{\\frac{1+3x}{1+x}} =(1+3x)^{\\frac12}(1+x)^{-\\frac12}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =(1+\\tfrac32x-\\tfrac98x^2+\\ldots)(1-\\tfrac12x+\\tfrac38x^2+\\ldots)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =1-\\tfrac12x+\\tfrac38x^2+\\tfrac32x-\\tfrac34x^2-\\tfrac98x^2\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =1+x-\\tfrac32x^2+\\ldots\\text{ as required}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Expansion valid for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|x|&lt;\\frac13\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.09-q9","number":9,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the first 3 terms in the expansion of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1-2x)^{\\frac12}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence, show that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\sqrt{1-2x}}{1+x}\\approx1-2x+\\frac32x^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li><li><p>State the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for which the expansion is valid.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1-2x)^{\\frac12} \\approx1+\\tfrac12(-2x)+\\tfrac12(\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac12)(-2x)^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx1-x-\\tfrac12x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\sqrt{1-2x}}{1+x}=(1-2x)^{\\frac12}(1+x)^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1+x)^{-1} \\approx1-x+\\tfrac12(-1)(-2)x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx1-x+x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\text{So } (1-x-\\tfrac12x^2+\\ldots)(1-x+x^2+\\ldots)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =1-x+x^2-x+x^2-x^3-\\tfrac12x^2+\\tfrac12x^3+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =1-2x+\\tfrac32x^2+\\ldots\\text{ as required}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|x|&lt;1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|2x|&lt;1\\Rightarrow|x|&lt;\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Expansion valid for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|x|&lt;\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.09-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>Given the binomial expansion</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1+qx)^p=1-2x+6x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are constants.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Hence state the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for which the expansion is valid.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"pq=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12(p)(p-1)q^2=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\Rightarrow\\tfrac12p^2q^2-\\tfrac12pq^2=6\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\Rightarrow2+q=6\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=-\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|4x|&lt;1\\Rightarrow|x|&lt;\\frac14\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.09-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>Given that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sqrt[3]{8-x}\\approx2-\\frac1{12}x+kx^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a constant.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>By using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the expansion, find an approximation to the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt[3]7\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(8-x)^{\\frac13}=8^{\\frac13}(1-\\frac18x)^{\\frac13}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx2[1-\\tfrac13(\\tfrac18x)+\\tfrac12\\times\\tfrac13(-\\tfrac23)(\\tfrac18x)^2+\\ldots]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx2-\\tfrac1{12}x-\\tfrac1{288}x^2+\\ldots\\text{ so }k=-\\tfrac1{288}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(8-1)^{\\frac13}\\approx2-\\frac1{12}-\\frac1{288}+\\ldots\\approx\\frac{551}{288}=1.913\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to 3 dp.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.09-q12","number":12,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>By using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac18\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the first three terms in the expansion of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{3-8x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, find an approximation for the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Explain whether your approximation is an under- or over-estimate.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3-8x)^{\\frac12}=3^{\\frac12}(1-\\frac83x)^{\\frac12}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\sqrt3[1-\\tfrac12(\\tfrac83x)+\\tfrac12\\times\\tfrac12(-\\tfrac12)(\\tfrac83x)^2+\\ldots]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\sqrt3[1-\\tfrac43x-\\tfrac89x^2+\\ldots]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3-8\\times\\frac18)^{\\frac12}=\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(3-8\\times\\tfrac18)^{\\frac12} \\approx\\sqrt3[1-\\tfrac43\\times\\tfrac18-\\tfrac89(\\tfrac18)^2+\\ldots]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\tfrac{59}{72}\\sqrt3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Overestimate since all the terms in the expansion except the first are negative.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.09-q13","number":13,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the terms up to and including the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> term in the expansion of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{\\sqrt{2-x}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol><p>Jenna considers using the values <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-\\frac65\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac15\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><p>Explain how she used the values to find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Which of the three values should not be used in the expansion?</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2-x)^{-\\frac12}=2^{-\\frac12}(1-\\frac12x)^{-\\frac12}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\tfrac1{\\sqrt2}[1-\\tfrac12(-\\tfrac12x)+\\tfrac12\\times(-\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac32)(-\\tfrac12x)^2+\\ldots]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =\\tfrac1{\\sqrt2}[1+\\tfrac14x+\\tfrac3{32}x^2+\\ldots]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =\\tfrac1{\\sqrt2}+\\tfrac1{4\\sqrt2}x+\\tfrac3{32\\sqrt2}x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =\\tfrac{\\sqrt2}2+\\tfrac{\\sqrt2}8x+\\tfrac{3\\sqrt2}{64}x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Let the expansion be <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{\\sqrt{2+3}}=\\frac1{\\sqrt5}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt5=5f(-3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-\\frac65\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{\\sqrt{2-\\frac65}}=\\frac{\\sqrt5}2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt5=2f(-\\frac65)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac15\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{\\sqrt{2-\\frac15}}=\\frac{\\sqrt5}3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt5=3f(\\frac15)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Since it is valid for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|\\frac12x|&lt;1\\Rightarrow|x|&lt;2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> may not be used.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.09-q14","number":14,"question":"<p>By considering the first three terms in the expansion of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{\\sqrt{7-x}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, find an approximation for the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(7-x)^{-\\frac12}=7^{-\\frac12}(1-\\frac17x)^{-\\frac12}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\tfrac1{\\sqrt7}[1-\\tfrac12(-\\tfrac17x)+\\tfrac12\\times(-\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac32)(-\\tfrac17x)^2+\\ldots]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =\\tfrac1{\\sqrt7}[1+\\tfrac1{14}x+\\tfrac3{392}x^2+\\ldots]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =\\tfrac1{\\sqrt7}+\\tfrac1{14\\sqrt7}x+\\tfrac3{392\\sqrt7}x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|\\frac17x|&lt;1\\Rightarrow|x|&lt;7\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(7-4)^{-\\frac12}=\\tfrac1{\\sqrt3}\\approx\\tfrac1{\\sqrt7}+\\tfrac1{14\\sqrt7}\\times4+\\tfrac3{392\\sqrt7}\\times4^2\\approx\\tfrac{69}{49\\sqrt7}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt3\\approx\\frac{49\\sqrt7}{69}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.09-q15","number":15,"question":"<p>The graph below shows <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sqrt{1-x^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.09/questions/assets/diagrams/209-q15.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>By considering the graph of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1+\\frac12x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span> explain why this is not a correct expansion of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{1-x^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>With each additional term the approximation should get closer to the exact result within the range of validity. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=1+\\frac12x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a positive quadratic graph so this means the second term increases in value and is further away from the graph of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{1-x^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> than <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.09-q16","number":16,"question":"<p>Find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> given</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{a+bx}{\\sqrt{9-x}}=1-\\frac{11}{18}x-\\frac7{216}x^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are constants.</p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(9-x)^{-\\frac12}=\\frac13(1-\\frac19x)^{-\\frac12}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\tfrac13[1-\\tfrac12(-\\tfrac19x)+\\tfrac12\\times(-\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac32)(-\\tfrac19x)^2+\\ldots]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\tfrac13[1+\\tfrac1{18}x+\\tfrac1{216}x^2+\\ldots]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\tfrac13+\\tfrac1{54}x+\\tfrac1{648}x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" (a+bx)(\\tfrac13+\\tfrac1{54}x+\\tfrac1{648}x^2-\\tfrac5{34992}x^3+\\ldots)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =1-\\tfrac{11}{18}x-\\tfrac7{216}x^2-\\tfrac{31}{11664}x^3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac3{54}+\\frac13b=-\\frac{11}{18}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.09-q17","number":17,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the first 4 terms in the expansion of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1+px)^{\\frac12}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a constant</p></li></ol><p>Given for the constant term <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1+qx)(1+px)^{\\frac12}=1-4x-14x^2+16x^3-\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><p>find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1+px)^{\\frac12} =1+\\tfrac12px+\\tfrac12\\times\\tfrac12(-\\tfrac12)p^2x^2+\\tfrac16\\times\\tfrac12(-\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac32)p^3x^3+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =1+\\tfrac12px-\\tfrac18p^2x^2+\\tfrac1{16}p^3x^3+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1+qx)(1+\\frac12px-\\frac18p^2x^2+\\frac1{16}p^3x^3+\\ldots)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-4=\\frac12p+q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-14=-\\frac18p^2+\\frac12pq\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-14=-\\frac18p^2+\\frac12p(-4-\\frac12p)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac38p^2+2p-14=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=-\\frac{28}3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. And <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q=\\frac23\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q=-6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. But considering <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> term: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\frac18p^2q+\\frac1{16}p^3=-14\" data-display=\"false\"></span> shows <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q=-6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.09-q18","number":18,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the first 4 terms in the expansion of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1-x)^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2+3x+4x^2+5x^3+\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{a-x}{(b-x)^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers to be found.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1-x)^{-2} \\approx1-2(-x)+\\tfrac12(-2)(-3)(-x)^2+\\tfrac16(-2)(-3)(-4)(-x)^3+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx1+2x+3x^2+4x^3+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(b-x)^{-2}=b^{-2}(1-\\frac1bx)^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\tfrac1{b^2}[1+\\tfrac2bx+\\tfrac3bx^2+\\tfrac4bx^3+\\ldots]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\tfrac1{b^2}+\\tfrac2{b^3}x+\\tfrac3{b^3}x^2+\\tfrac4{b^3}x^3+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2+3x+4x^2+5x^3+\\ldots=(a-x)(\\tfrac1{b^2}+\\tfrac2{b^3}x+\\tfrac3{b^3}x^2+\\tfrac4{b^3}x^3+\\ldots)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Which gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac a{b^2}=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{2a}{b^3}-\\frac1{b^2}=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac4b-\\frac1{b^2}=3\\Rightarrow3b^2-4b+1=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. With <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b=\\frac13\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. But <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Or</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" 2+3x+4x^2+5x^3+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =1+2x+3x^2+4x^3+\\ldots+1+x+x^2+x^3+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =(1-x)^{-2}+(1-x)^{-1}=\\frac1{(1-x)^2}+\\frac1{1-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =\\frac1{(1-x)^2}+\\frac{1-x}{(1-x)^2}=\\frac{2-x}{(1-x)^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.09-q19","number":19,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q19--Q21: Partial Fractions</strong> It is known that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{2-5x}{(x-1)(2x-1)},\\qquad x\\neq1,\\ x\\neq\\frac12\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>can be expressed in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac A{x-1}+\\frac B{2x-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Hence find the first three terms in the expansion of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{2-5x}{(x-1)(2x-1)}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{2-5x}{(x-1)(2x-1)}=\\frac A{x-1}+\\frac B{2x-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2-5x=A(2x-1)+B(x-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2=-A-B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-5=2A+B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=-3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{2-5x}{(x-1)(2x-1)}=-\\frac3{x-1}+\\frac1{2x-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1-x)^{-1} \\approx1-(-x)+\\tfrac12(-1)(-2)(-x)^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx1+x+x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(-1+2x)^{-1} =-(1-2x)^{-1}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx-[1+2x+(2x)^2+\\ldots]\\approx-1-2x-4x^2-\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"-\\frac3{x-1}+\\frac1{2x-1} \\approx3(1-x)^{-1}+(-1+2x)^{-1}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx3(1+x+x^2+\\ldots)+(-1-2x-4x^2-\\ldots)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Hence <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{2-5x}{(x-1)(2x-1)}\\approx2+x-x^2-\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.09-q20","number":20,"question":"<p>By expressing</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{11x+5}{(5x+1)(x+3)},\\qquad x\\neq-\\frac15,\\ x\\neq-\\frac13\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac A{5x+1}+\\frac B{x+3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the first 3 terms in the binomial expansion of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{11x+5}{(5x+1)(x+3)}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>State the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for which the expansion is valid.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{11x+5}{(5x+1)(x+3)}=\\frac A{5x+1}+\\frac B{x+3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"11x+5=A(x+3)+B(5x+1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"11=A+5B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5=3A+B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{11x+5}{(5x+1)(x+3)}=\\frac1{5x+1}+\\frac2{x+3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1+5x)^{-1} \\approx1-1(5x)+\\tfrac12(-1)(-2)(5x)^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx1-5x+25x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(3+x)^{-1} =\\tfrac13(1+\\tfrac13x)^{-1}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\tfrac13[1-1(\\tfrac13x)+\\tfrac12(-1)(-2)(\\tfrac13x)^2+\\ldots]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\tfrac13-\\tfrac19x+\\tfrac1{27}x^2-\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac1{5x+1}+\\frac2{x+3} \\approx(1+5x)^{-1}+2(3+x)^{-1}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx(1-5x+25x^2+\\ldots)+2(\\tfrac13-\\tfrac19x+\\tfrac1{27}x^2-\\ldots)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Hence <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{11x+5}{(5x+1)(x+3)}\\approx\\frac53-\\frac{47}9x+\\frac{677}{27}x^2-\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|5x|&lt;1\\Rightarrow|x|&lt;\\frac15\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|\\frac13x|&lt;1\\Rightarrow|x|&lt;3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|x|&lt;\\frac15\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.09-q21","number":21,"question":"<p>By expressing</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{9x^2-5x+2}{(x+1)(3x+1)^2},\\qquad x\\neq-1,\\ x\\neq-\\frac13\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>as partial fractions,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the first 3 terms in the binomial expansion of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{9x^2-5x+2}{(x+1)(3x+1)^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>State the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for which the expansion is valid.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{9x^2-5x+2}{(x+1)(3x+1)^2}=\\frac A{x+1}+\\frac B{3x+1}+\\frac C{(3x+1)^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"9x^2-5x+2=A(3x+1)^2+B(3x+1)(x+1)+C(x+1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"9=9A+3B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-5=6A+4B+C\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2=A+B+C\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{9x^2-5x+2}{(x+1)(3x+1)^2}=\\frac4{x+1}-\\frac9{3x+1}+\\frac7{(3x+1)^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1+x)^{-1} \\approx1-1(x)+\\tfrac12(-1)(-2)(x)^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx1-x+x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1+3x)^{-1} \\approx1-3x+9x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1+3x)^{-2} \\approx1-2(3x)+\\tfrac12(-2)(-3)(3x)^2+\\ldots\\approx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\frac4{x+1}-\\frac9{3x+1}+\\frac7{(3x+1)^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =4(x+1)^{-1}-9(3x+1)^{-1}+7(3x+1)^{-2}\\quad1-6x+27x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Hence</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{9x^2-5x+2}{(x+1)(3x+1)^2} \\approx4(1-x+x^2+\\ldots)-9(1-3x+9x^2+\\ldots)+7(1-6x+27x^2+\\ldots)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx2-19x+112x^2-\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|3x|&lt;1\\Rightarrow|x|&lt;\\frac13\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|x|&lt;1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|x|&lt;\\frac13\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.09-q22","number":22,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q22: Integration of Polynomials</strong></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the first three terms in the expansion of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{\\sqrt{9-x}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence find an approximation for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\int_0^1\\frac1{\\sqrt{9-x^2}}\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(9-x)^{-\\frac12}=\\frac13(1-\\frac19x)^{-\\frac12}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\tfrac13[1-\\tfrac12(-\\tfrac19x)+\\tfrac12\\times(-\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac32)(-\\tfrac19x)^2+\\ldots]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\tfrac13[1+\\tfrac1{18}x+\\tfrac1{216}x^2+\\ldots]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx\\tfrac13+\\tfrac1{54}x+\\tfrac1{648}x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(9-x^2)^{-\\frac12}\\approx\\frac13+\\frac1{54}x^2+\\frac1{648}x^4+\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int_0^1\\frac1{\\sqrt{9-x^2}}\\,dx \\approx[\\tfrac13x+\\tfrac1{162}x^3+\\tfrac1{3240}x^4]_0^1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =(\\tfrac13+\\tfrac1{162}+\\tfrac1{3240})-(0)=\\tfrac{367}{1080}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.09-q23","number":23,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q23: Radians</strong> A 1 radian sector of a circle has area <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x+2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Show that for small values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the radius is given by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r\\approx2+px-qx^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are constants to be found.</p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=\\frac12r^2\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x+2=\\frac12\\times r^2\\times1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=\\sqrt{2x+4}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4+2x)^{\\frac12}=4^{\\frac12}(1+\\frac12x)^{\\frac12}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r \\approx2[1+\\tfrac12(\\tfrac12x)+\\tfrac12(\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac12)(\\tfrac12x)^2+\\ldots]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\approx2+\\tfrac12x-\\tfrac1{16}x^2+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]}]